{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Persistence is Key"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Now, The Next Step "}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe issues relating to money, in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le10ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Passive Voice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " In English, all sentences are in either \u201cactive\u201d or \u201cpassive\u201d voice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The active voice focuses on the thing which is doing the action (i.e. the subject of the sentence) and the thing receiving the action (i.e. the object). Most sentences in English are in the active voice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">We</span> need to do <span class=\"underline\">a lot of research</span> before the interview.</span> </li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use the passive when the \u2018doer' (agent) of the action it not so important. We are not interested in knowing who did the action. Our attention is on the object. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">A lot of research </span> needs to be done before the interview.</li> </ul></span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here's some more information about the passive of modal verbs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol type=\"a\"><li>The Passive is formed by [thing receiving the action] + be + past participle + (by) + (thing doing the action)</li> <li>The passive can be used when the \u201cdoer\u201d is unknown, irrelevant, or you want to be vague about who is responsible for the action. </li>  <li>You can also use the passive to talk about a general truth. </li> </ol>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "This will be useful when you <span class=\"underline\">are being asked </span> questions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The job specifications <span class=\"underline\">should be studied </span> carefully. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Questions about certain skills or experience <span class=\"underline\">are going to be asked</span> . "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Punctuality <span class=\"underline\">is seen </span> as a sign of professionalism."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Before the <span class=\"underline\">interview is finished</span> , ask a few smart final questions."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Causative With Get/Have"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use a causative verb when you want to talk about something that someone else did for you or for another person. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it themselves. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the causative verbs <span class=\"strong\">get</span>, <span class=\"strong\">make</span>  and <span class=\"strong\">have</span>  when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li><span class=\"italic\">His bad experience made me want to write and research more on this. </span> </li> </ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the causative is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "have + person + verb<br/>make + person + verb <br/> get + person + to + verb "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes, you use <span class=\"italic\">get </span> when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something.<span class=\"italic\"> Have </span> is a little more neutral."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Make them believe you by being yourself. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Get a friend to ask you questions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Then, have them give you feedback on your answers. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I hope the research has him succeed in his next interview. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to prioritize "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to decide in what order you should do things, based on how important or urgent they are "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Preparation and rehearsal are to be prioritized."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about getting a job."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "feedback"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "comments about how well or badly someone is doing "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Have them give you feedback on your answers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "up your sleeve"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have secret plans or ideas"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Have two to three successful stories up your sleeve."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "punctuality"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "arriving on time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Punctuality is seen as a sign of professionalism."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "skill"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability to do something well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Questions about certain skills or experience are going to be asked."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to ace"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do very well in something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Ace your interview and get hired! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "self-confidence"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the feeling that you can do things well "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to display the right amount of self-confidence. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob05aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "research"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the detailed study of something in order to discover new facts"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope this research helps him."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob05aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and find a job posting."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Highlight all the skills and qualifications they ask for."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner think of and write down 5 or 6 questions an interviewer would ask (about prior experience, strengths and education)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give the questions to your partner who will act as the interviewer."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use your highlighted sheet to help you answer the questions."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research job postings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify skills and qualifications for the job"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write questions based on the job posting."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask and answer questions in a job interview."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can exchange complex information about work."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain how to pr